Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: qcom-geni-serial: clear S_IRQ status in stop_rx_dma to prevent suspend IRQ storm

During system suspend, uart_suspend_port() sets uport->suspended = 1,
acquires the port spinlock with IRQs disabled, calls ops->stop_rx()
(qcom_geni_serial_stop_rx_dma() on DMA UARTs such as the WCN6855
Bluetooth UART), and then unlocks IRQs before calling ops->shutdown()
(which disables uport->irq).

qcom_geni_serial_stop_rx_dma() issues geni_se_cancel_s_cmd(), which
asserts S_CMD_CANCEL_EN in SE_GENI_S_IRQ_STATUS, but only clears
SE_DMA_RX_IRQ_CLR and never clears SE_GENI_S_IRQ_CLEAR (unlike
qcom_geni_serial_stop_rx_fifo()).  As soon as uart_suspend_port()
re-enables IRQs, the level-triggered GENI SE IRQ fires while
uport->suspended is already 1; qcom_geni_serial_isr() returns IRQ_NONE
without clearing the status register, causing an interrupt storm until
the kernel reports "irq N: nobody cared" and permanently disables the
Bluetooth UART IRQ until reboot.

Clear SE_GENI_S_IRQ_STATUS via SE_GENI_S_IRQ_CLEAR in
qcom_geni_serial_stop_rx_dma() after cancelling/aborting the secondary
command.

---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -992,6 +992,7 @@
 static void qcom_geni_serial_stop_rx_dma(struct uart_port *uport)
 {
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = to_dev_port(uport);
+	u32 s_irq_status;
 	bool done;
 
 	if (!qcom_geni_serial_secondary_active(uport))
@@ -1013,6 +1014,8 @@
 				uport->membase + SE_DMA_RX_IRQ_CLR);
 	}
 
+	s_irq_status = readl(uport->membase + SE_GENI_S_IRQ_STATUS);
+	writel(s_irq_status, uport->membase + SE_GENI_S_IRQ_CLEAR);
 }
 
 static void qcom_geni_serial_start_rx_dma(struct uart_port *uport)
